# =============================================================================
# .Renviron.example
# =============================================================================
# Template for local, machine-specific environment variables used by this
# project. Copy this file to ".Renviron" (same folder, no ".example" suffix)
# and fill in your own values. ".Renviron" is gitignored — it never gets
# committed, so each user/machine keeps its own copy.
#
#   cp .Renviron.example .Renviron
#
# R reads .Renviron automatically at startup when you open this project
# (restart your R session / RStudio after editing it for changes to apply).
# =============================================================================

# Absolute path to the folder containing the raw CoLaus/OsteoLaus CSV files
# (see 01_data/README.md for the exact list of expected files).
#
# Optional: if this is not set, 02_scripts/_targets.R falls back to the
# "01_data" folder inside this project. Set DAIRY_DATA_DIR only if you keep
# the raw data somewhere else (e.g. a synced cloud-storage folder, as in the
# example below).
DAIRY_DATA_DIR=/path/to/your/Dairy_sarcopenia_data
